webCoRE dashboard - Docker
==========================

This builds a small Apache (httpd:2.4-alpine) container that serves the local
dashboard/ folder in this repo. Everything is baked into the image at build
time - there are no external files or host volumes to set up, so a fresh clone
builds and runs as-is.

Improvements from Public WebCoRE Interface
-----------
tl;dr App has been streamlined, bugs have been fixed, quality of life improvements, and now supports arbitrary endpoints (for use with reverse proxies). No changes are required in the Hubitat Apps.

- Fix: Mobile experience is improved (drag and drop, right click works).
- Fix: keep linebreaks on comments when displayed.
- Fix: Ordering is retained when drag/drop of long lists.
- Fix: Expression outputs now wrap so you can see everything and can also copy the output.
- Fix: Device filter is retained after selecting a device in the device picker.
- Fix: Expression editor no longer overflows and expands properly.
- Fix: No scrollbar on left nav menu unless needed.
- Feature: Variables can be duplicated.
- Feature: Login without using the webcore code by directly providing the link, so there are zero external cloud dependencies.
- Feature: Switch between local and cloud endpoints.
- Feature: Show cloud and local execution URIs for each piston.
- Feature: Set a default category and select the category you want the piston in during creation.
- Feature: Supports arbitrary hubitat endpoints (e.g., use a reverse proxy). HTTP/HTTPS must match.
- Feature: All dependencies are local (except piston backup).
- Feature: Docker build now minifies all assets and runs on Alpine
- Feature: Added debug view in settings to see all local state.
- Feature: Enabled Variables, drag/drop and advanced statements by default.
- Removed Google Ads, Google Maps, Dashboards, Fuel Streams and device list in piston editor.
- Minor UX color improvements for consistency.

Quick start
-----------
    docker compose up -d --build

Then open http://localhost:8090

Endpoint to Hub ID mapping
--------------------------
Set `WEBCORE_ENDPOINT_HUB_ID_MAP` to a JSON object when a local endpoint needs
to be associated with its Hubitat cloud Hub ID. Endpoint matching ignores case
and trailing slashes. Browser settings entered under Settings > General take
precedence over this mapping.

  WEBCORE_ENDPOINT_HUB_ID_MAP={"https://hubitat.example.com":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"} docker compose up -d --build

Multiple endpoints may be included in the same JSON object. With `docker run`,
pass the value using `-e WEBCORE_ENDPOINT_HUB_ID_MAP=...`.

The dashboard is an AngularJS HTML5-mode single-page app served from the site
root. Deep links / refreshes are handled by dashboard/.htaccess (mod_rewrite),
which is enabled in the Dockerfile.

Without docker compose
----------------------
    docker build -t webcore-dashboard .
    docker run -d -p 8090:80 webcore-dashboard

Notes
-----
- The container serves plain HTTP on port 80 (published as 8090 on the host).
  TLS is expected to be terminated upstream by a reverse proxy / load balancer.
- To proxy your local hub's API through this origin (same-origin, no CORS),
  edit webcore-apache.conf and uncomment / adjust the ProxyPass lines, then
  rebuild.